@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# 0002 — Reservation contract with the cart service
+
+Status: accepted (2026-10-29)
+
+## Decision
+- **Partial holds.** `reserve` holds `min(requested, available)` per line and
+  omits lines with nothing available; it fails with `InsufficientStock` only if
+  nothing at all can be held. Bad input rejects the whole request.
+  (`place_order` stays all-or-nothing.)
+- **Idempotency.** Keys are global and permanent for the repository's life. A
+  replay with the same warehouse and the same *requested* items returns the
+  original reservation as it is now (no new hold, no TTL extension), even when
+  it is finished. A different request under a used key raises
+  `IdempotencyConflict`. Failed calls do not consume a key. Input validation
+  runs before the key lookup, so invalid input under a used key raises the
+  validation error rather than `IdempotencyConflict` (owner: either is
+  acceptable; validation-first kept).
+- **Confirm** honours the hold without re-checking stock and is idempotent:
+  confirming a confirmed reservation returns the same order at any time.
+- **TTL** defaults to 20 minutes from creation.
+
+## Consequences
+The cart service must compare `Reservation.items` with what it asked for to
+detect a partial hold. Changing any of these rules changes the cart service's
+retry behaviour and needs coordination with it.
